# Requests to try the API from Visual Studio, Rider or the VS Code REST Client extension.
# Start the API first: dotnet run --project backend/VehicleExplorer.Api

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### All makes (over 12,000, sorted by name)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/makes/GetMakes

### Vehicle types for HONDA (make id 474)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/makes/GetVehicleTypes?makeId=474

### Models for HONDA in 2015, filtered to Passenger Car (vehicleType is optional)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/makes/GetModels?makeId=474&year=2015&vehicleType=Passenger%20Car

### Empty vehicleType is treated as "all types"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/makes/GetModels?makeId=474&year=2015&vehicleType=

### Invalid year returns 400 ProblemDetails
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/makes/GetModels?makeId=474&year=1980

### Missing makeId returns 400 ProblemDetails
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/makes/GetVehicleTypes

### Unknown API URL returns 404, not index.html
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/unknown
